  "known_limitations": [
    "no destination overload: destination U after migration stays in [0.47, 0.90]; any prediction at U >= 1 is an extrapolation",
    "measured loads are below the planned levels: hot-switch share (moderate, high, peak) and the 0.75 destination level of the hot_switch workload (see measured_vs_planned); use the measured values, never the plan",
    "the source side is dominated by the workload trend in burst, gradual and oscillating; NO_OP controls exist only for the middle phase of each workload (8 per workload: 2 per destination level and direction)",
    "official collection has no failure injection; RESTORED behaviour is covered by the smoke rollback attempt only (evidence/week11/smoke_rollback.json)",
    "after a migration the twin needs 4-55 s to give 5 Hard-Gate-valid snapshots again (stepped around 5, 15 and 35 s); mechanism to confirm"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "phase early includes the workload warm-up: delta_*_mean and delta_*_last can differ (keep both, Week 12 chooses)",
    "every attempt is kept, none imputed or dropped; invalid attempts would stay in the dataset with valid = false"
  ],
  "open_decisions": [
    "overload region (U >= 1): keep v1 as is (chosen to close Week 11) and ask the advisor at the start of Week 12 whether to collect a separate stress dataset (destination 0.85 / 0.95, hot_switch only) or to check it in the closed-loop experiments"
